From bd9a36def55cde1c478136b31bf3c7c3a717d520 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:08:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: hand the munchkin turn to recovery while poisoned or
 hallucinating

Munchkin start mode keeps exploring by shuttling between known stairs.
Stair travel does not age the world clock: entering a level grants
minimum move energy and the world tick is skipped during level
generation, so a poisoned or hallucinating Borg that stair-cycles can
never let those timed ailments run out. The munchkin branch also runs
before the ordinary dungeon think, so its poison and hallucination
recovery handling is never reached.

Bail out of munchkin mode while BI_ISPOISONED or BI_ISIMAGE is active,
in the branch's existing early-bail sequence: the ordinary recovery
path takes the turn, ages the world clock normally, and the ailments
wear off (walking and resting clear them). The clean control confirms
munchkin play is unchanged.

Native fixture: Human Warrior, seed 1045, depth 9, known underfoot up
stair plus a down stair three tiles east; ailments enter through the
real timed-effect API. Original: the ailed Borg power-climbs
(stair_directed=1). Corrected: the ailed Borg hands the turn to
recovery (stair_directed=0); the clean control still climbs in both.
Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#403.

(cherry picked from commit d92e06c3f964e4bba19642288ded1b331a327109)
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
index a3dd50f89..2ab8469f0 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
@@ -458,6 +458,17 @@ static bool borg_think_dungeon_munchkin(void)
         return false;
     }
 
+    /* Not while poisoned or hallucinating. Stair travel does not age the
+     * world clock (level entry grants minimum move energy and the world
+     * tick is skipped during level generation), so these timed ailments
+     * can never wear off while the borg shuttles between stairs. Leave
+     * them to the ordinary recovery path, which ages turns normally. */
+    if (borg.trait[BI_ISPOISONED] || borg.trait[BI_ISIMAGE]) {
+        borg_note("# Leaving munchkin Mode. (Poisoned or Hallucinating)");
+        borg.munchkin_mode = false;
+        return false;
+    }
+
     /* if borg is just starting on this level, he may not
      * know that a stair is under him.  Cheat to see if one is
      * there
-- 
